Package: bande-firefox-esr-settings
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: firefox-esr, ${misc:Depends}
Enhances: firefox-esr
Description: Bande's browser settings for firefox-esr
 Preferences and enterprise policies that give Debian's firefox-esr the
 settings of Bande's Browser: no telemetry, studies or remote experiments, no
 sponsored content or recommendations, no Remote Settings downloads, no
 Safe Browsing or network geolocation, no prefetching, DRM content and web
 push off by default, and the tab strip in the title bar.
 .
 Settings are applied system-wide. Users can change those that are not locked
 in about:config; a policies.json under /etc/firefox/policies replaces the one
 this package installs.
